body.end_state:
Grounded numbers become honest pictures — the pipeline stops being two halves.

The data half is built and stays built: versioned NASA Exoplanet Archive snapshots, per-planet observer-conditions records where every value carries a firm_physics / reasoned_inference / speculative tier, and a claim-grounding ledger that refuses to write a record it cannot source (154 regression tests green). The visual half is still at zero. The 2026-08-11 horizon recorded it as "opened", but the task that carried it (8142b0fa) was closed as skipped on 2026-08-12 — "we are super busy with other things this week" — not delivered, so the 2/2 reading was a false green.

The new bar is that a grounded record becomes a picture as honest as the record:
- a renderer consumes the observer_conditions record itself, not a hand-built scene, so every visible feature — sky colour, the star's angular size, horizon, illumination — traces to a numbered field through docs/visual_mapping_logic.md;
- the frame carries its own uncertainty: a speculative sky is labelled speculative in the image, not only in the JSON;
- rendering refuses a record whose grounding ledger is not fully supported, exactly as writing one already does;
- output is reproducible — same record and same pipeline version give the same image, asserted by test, so a frame can be cited in an episode the way a number can;
- the two derivation paths converge on the grounded pipeline: the Python snapshot → observer-conditions → grounding chain is what the renderer reads, retiring TheNexus astro-parameters.js scene export as the source of visual truth, whatever the renderer itself turns out to be (a matplotlib/Pillow composition, the browser viewer, or Unreal).

Success looks like: Robert names any confirmed host system, runs the pipeline end to end, and gets episode-usable stills of both the system in motion and the view from the surface — with nothing on screen that the ledger cannot source, and every uncertain feature labelled as such.

This end state is expected to EVOLVE: when all three criteria below pass and one episode's visuals come out of the pipeline unretouched, the next horizon is production cadence — episode assembly and publishing rhythm — not visual fidelity.

Criteria note: this horizon deliberately declares no task_set criterion. Closing a board task as "skipped" sets its status to completed, which silently satisfies a task_set criterion — that is precisely how the previous horizon read 2/2 with nothing rendered. Every criterion here is an artifact-observable command.

